  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "This smoke detector can sound the alarm before flames are visible. Inside this photoelectric detector, smoke reveals itself by scattering a hidden beam of light. In clear air, an LED sends light across a dark chamber. The light sensor sits off to one side, so the straight beam normally misses it. When smoke enters, tiny particles scatter some of that light toward the sensor. The sensor signal rises and the electronics trigger the loud alarm. It is especially useful for slow, smoldering fires that produce visible smoke. So the detector does not smell smoke, it notices smoke scattering light into its sensor.",
  "mean_word_probability": 0.9793650016091228,
